          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "This morning, you explore the German Colonies of the region. Colonia Independencia was founded on January 17th, 1919, by German settlers who arrived after the First World War. They brought their culture, their architecture, and their traditions with them, and the area still carries that heritage today. It is particularly famous for its artisanal wine production, and visitors come from across the country to taste the local wines and experience the enduring German spirit of the place.\n\nLunch is enjoyed at Tylinsky. After the meal, you set off back to Asunción."
    },
